From a969c6ea0cd5f6bcfbe7e3af21727906f4ff1a80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 19:50:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 411/415] resolve: `Self::Variant` keeps the impl type's
 parameters on the variant node

jaq-core 3.1.2 (jaq) load/parse.rs:863 `Self::Or => Self::Alt.precedence() + 1`
inside `impl<S> prec_climb::Op for BinaryOp<S>`:
    error:0: Failed to infer type _/*62*/ in &BinaryOp<_>

The "UFCS of enum variant converted to Generic" rewrite of `<Self>::Variant`
appended the variant to the impl type's path and left `Self`'s `<S>` on the
enum node. HIR lowering reads only the last node's arguments (a written
`BinaryOp::<S>::Alt` has them moved to the variant node by
Resolve_Absolute_Path_BindAbsolute), so typeck saw `BinaryOp::Alt`, gave the
enum fresh type variables, and the `&self` receiver bound nothing.

The rewrite now moves the enum node's arguments to the variant node.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.1
---

diff --git a/src/resolve/absolute.cpp b/src/resolve/absolute.cpp
index 7286bbf9..865b9bbe 100644
--- a/src/resolve/absolute.cpp
+++ b/src/resolve/absolute.cpp
@@ -2138,7 +2138,13 @@ void Resolve_Absolute_Path(/*const*/ Context& context, const Span& sp, Context::
                                 unsigned idx = it - enm.variants().begin();
                                 auto p2 = p.m_bindings.type.path + name;
                                 auto new_path = std::move(p);
+                                // The variant carries the enum's parameters (as `Resolve_Absolute_Path_BindAbsolute` moves
+                                // them for a written `Enum::<T>::Variant`): HIR lowering reads only the last node's
+                                // arguments, so leaving `Self`'s on the enum node gave `BinaryOp::Alt` fresh type
+                                // variables (jaq-core 3.1.2 `Self::Alt.precedence()` in `impl<S> Op for BinaryOp<S>`).
+                                auto enum_args = std::move(new_path.nodes().back().args());
                                 new_path.append(name);
+                                new_path.nodes().back().args() = std::move(enum_args);
                                 if( it->m_data.is_Struct() ) {
                                     new_path.m_bindings.type.set(p2, AST::PathBinding_Type::make_EnumVar({ &enm, idx }));
                                 }
